          "path": "_m/w/x/4/g/beijing-dongyue-temple-wp/beijing-2006-1-29.jpg",
          "filename": "Beijing 2006 1-29.jpg",
          "caption": "Dong Yue Miao, Beijing\nThis Daoist temple, founded in the Yuan dynasty, is dedicated to Yama as Dong Yue, the God of the Mountain, and to the cult of the dead at Mount Tai. After falling into disrepair, the temple was restored\nand reopened in the late 1990s.\n\nThe temple's main gate is seen here. The photo looks north, up the main axis of the temple.",
          "alt": "Dong Yue Miao, Beijing\nThis Daoist temple, founded in the Yuan dynasty, is dedicated to Yama as Dong Yue, the God of the Mountain, and to the cult of the dead at Mount Tai. After falling into disrepair, the temple was restored\nand reopened in the late 1990s.\n\nThe temple's main gate is seen here. The photo looks north, up the main axis of the temple.",
          "width": 2592,
          "height": 1944,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
